e. Extract or reuse the Software's code, assets, interface, data, or settings in another product.
f. Use or share another person's account or session, or let anyone use yours, or forge, replay, or alter requests to the
   Wave service, or use the service other than through the official Software.
g. Overload, scrape, probe, or interfere with the Wave service, or try to get around its rate limits or blocks.
h. Remove or change any copyright, license, or ownership notice.
i. Use the Software, or what you learn from it, to build or help build a competing product.
j. Publish or share tools, instructions, keys, or accounts that let others do any of the above.

Where the law of your country gives you a right that this section tries to take away (for example certain limited rights
